  "body": "Found while fixing #1056 point 2 (PR on branch `issue/1056-fidelity-unknown`).\n\nWhat happens: since project v59, every mesh of an older project without a recorded chord loads \"fidelity unknown\" (`model_fidelity::UNKNOWN_MM`) and the gate refuses its operations by name until the model is re-imported. That is the safe reading, but a model whose source file is gone, or whose mesh is exact (an STL/OBJ import, a mesh built in code), can then never post again without a re-import.\n\nExpected: an undoable command (e.g. `VouchModelFidelity`) that clears the mark for one model (and its from-model stock copies), stating in the history and on the model page who vouched; its MCP tool and script verb with it. Undo puts the mark back. It must never apply to a model whose chord is recorded coarse (#864) - only to the unknown sentinel.\n\nSafety floor: it changes what the gouge laws judge, so effort:high.\n\nDone means: the command, its MCP tool, a pin that a vouched model posts and its undo is refused again, and the model page offers it beside the \"Fidelity unknown\" line.\n\nPart of #1056 (follow-up).\n",
